Here is a **clean, step-by-step guide** for setting up Maven + TestNG project and running tests from terminal — exactly in the correct order and very easy to follow.

---

# ✅ **Steps to Configure Maven, Add Plugin & Run TestNG from Terminal**

---

## **🔹 Step 1 — Add Surefire Plugin in `pom.xml`**

This plugin tells Maven to run TestNG tests.


	<build>
		<plugins>
			<!-- Compiler Plugin -->
			<plugin>
				<groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
				<artifactId>maven-compiler-plugin</artifactId>
				<version>3.11.0</version>
				<configuration>
					<source>${maven.compiler.source}</source>
					<target>${maven.compiler.target}</target>
				</configuration>
			</plugin>

			<!-- Surefire Plugin -->
			<plugin>
				<groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
				<artifactId>maven-surefire-plugin</artifactId>
				<version>${surefire.version}</version>
				<configuration>
					<suiteXmlFiles>
						<suiteXmlFile>src/test/resources/testng.xml</suiteXmlFile>
					</suiteXmlFiles>
					<testFailureIgnore>false</testFailureIgnore>
				</configuration>
			</plugin>
		</plugins>
	</build>
</project>
---

## **🔹 Step 2 — Download & Install Apache Maven**

1. Go to Maven official site
   Download → **Binary Zip**
2. Extract it
3. Move folder to:

   ```
   C:\Program Files\apache-maven-3.xx
   ```

---

## **🔹 Step 3 — Add Maven to Eclipse**

1. Go to **Window → Preferences**
2. Select **Maven → Installations**
3. Click **Add**
4. Browse to:

   ```
   C:\Program Files\apache-maven-3.xx
   ```
5. Select the folder → OK
6. Tick ✔ that Maven installation → Apply → OK

---

## **🔹 Step 4 — Set Maven Environment Variable**

### 1️⃣ Add MAVEN_HOME

Control Panel → System → Advanced System Settings → Environment Variables → New

```
Variable name: MAVEN_HOME
Variable value: C:\Program Files\apache-maven-3.xx
```

### 2️⃣ Add Maven to PATH

Edit **Path** → Add

```
%MAVEN_HOME%\bin
```

---

## **🔹 Step 5 — Verify Maven Installation**

Open CMD and run:

```
mvn -v
```

If output shows Maven version → it's installed correctly.

---

## **🔹 Step 6 — Go to Your Project Folder**

Example:

```
cd C:\Users\HP\eclipse-workspace\seleniumframeworkproject
```

---

## **🔹 Step 7 — Run Maven Commands**

### 🔸 Clean project

```
mvn clean
```

### 🔸 Run TestNG test suite

```
mvn clean test
```

Maven will automatically run your `testng.xml` from:

```
src/test/resources/testng.xml
```

---

cmd to rum xml:- mvn clean test -DsuiteXmlFile=src/test/resources/testng.xml



# ✔ Done!

Now your Maven + TestNG setup is 100% correct and terminal execution works.
